<http://example.com/fhir/hl7.fhir.eu.health-data-api.test/ImplementationGuide/hl7.fhir.eu.health-data-api.test> a fhir:ImplementationGuide ;
  fhir:nodeRole fhir:treeRoot ;
  fhir:id [ fhir:v "hl7.fhir.eu.health-data-api.test"] ; # 
  fhir:language [ fhir:v "en"] ; # 
  fhir:text [
     fhir:status [ fhir:v "generated" ] ;
     fhir:div [ fhir:v "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\" xml:lang=\"en\" lang=\"en\"><p class=\"res-header-id\"><b>Generated Narrative: ImplementationGuide hl7.fhir.eu.health-data-api.test</b></p><a name=\"hl7.fhir.eu.health-data-api.test\"> </a><a name=\"hchl7.fhir.eu.health-data-api.test\"> </a><div style=\"display: inline-block; background-color: #fbffeb; padding: 6px; margin: 4px; border: 1px solid #8da1b4; border-radius: 5px; line-height: 60%\"><p style=\"margin-bottom: 0px\">Language: en</p></div><h2>EUHealthDataApiTesting</h2><p>The official URL for this implementation guide is: </p><pre>http://example.com/fhir/hl7.fhir.eu.health-data-api.test/ImplementationGuide/hl7.fhir.eu.health-data-api.test</pre><div><p>A demonstration IG that declares, as TestPlan resources and Gherkin feature files, the conformance tests for the six actors of the EU Health Data API IG (EHDS Annex II): Document Publisher, Document Access Provider (with the Document Submission Option), Document Consumer, grouped Document Publisher/Access Provider, Resource Access Provider and Resource Consumer. The IG states its requirements as capabilitystatement-expectation extensions rather than profile obligations, so every test case is traceable to the CapabilityStatement expectation it tests.</p>\n</div></div>"^^rdf:XMLLiteral ]
  ] ; # 
  fhir:url [
     fhir:v "http://example.com/fhir/hl7.fhir.eu.health-data-api.test/ImplementationGuide/hl7.fhir.eu.health-data-api.test"^^xsd:anyURI ;
     fhir:l <http://example.com/fhir/hl7.fhir.eu.health-data-api.test/ImplementationGuide/hl7.fhir.eu.health-data-api.test>
  ] ; # 
